      "summary": "Tuesday 06/10 We are open today with more spring weather. We are expecting a mainly fine day with northerly winds. Winds are forecast to increase later in the day. Spring snow conditions continue with a firm snowpack start, becoming soft and springy throughout the day. Snow coverage is still excellent and the groomers have been busy laying down lots of cord overnight and this morning. Main Basin and Valley will be open from 9am to 4:30pm. Captains, T-Bar and Soho open from 9:30. The snow is melting fast down low and Valley View will be open for uplift only today from 9-11am. You can still park at Valley and then ski back to your car at the end of your day. The ANC Slopestyle competition is running today in Big Bucks. Come watch local talent throw down with some of the worlds best. The halfpipe and platter will be opening at 10am today so we can salt the pipe before it gets ridden. Friendly reminder, we have also switched to our spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule! Pine Trees Shuttle - Up: 9am | 10am | 11am Down: 2pm | 3pm | 4pm | 4:45pm Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 7 / 10 Runs Open - / 38 Percent open 60 %",
